  master and run the script again. }

{ Integration tests of SASL against the real broker of
  docker/docker-compose.yml: SASL_PLAINTEXT on 9096, SASL_SSL on 9097 (the
  TLS of pascal-common-faa's test PKI), and 9098, SASL_PLAINTEXT whose
  sessions last 2 s (connections.max.reauth.ms, KIP-368). Users: PLAIN
  alice / alice-secret (JAAS), SCRAM-SHA-256 bob / bob-secret (created when
  the storage was formatted, 8192 iterations).

  - The producer and the consumer through each listener and mechanism
    (SASL_PLAINTEXT and SASL_SSL, PLAIN and SCRAM-SHA-256): keyed records
    produced and polled back where the producer's reports said.
  - What the broker answers, as Kafka.Connection reads it: a wrong password
    is EKafkaAuthentication with SASL_AUTHENTICATION_FAILED and the broker's
    message (PLAIN and SCRAM); a SASL client on the PLAINTEXT listener gets
    ILLEGAL_SASL_STATE; a client without SASL on a SASL listener is hung up
    on at its first request after ApiVersions.
  - KIP-368: the broker gives a 2 s session; the connection is due for
    re-authentication between 1.7 and 1.9 s; the cluster then hands out a
    new connection, and the broker closes the old one at its next request
    once the session is over. A producer and a consumer keep working across
    several sessions.

  Waiting for time to pass. A session's end is the point of the KIP-368
  tests, so they wait for it: in a consumer's Poll on the PLAINTEXT
  listener, which the broker answers when records come or its MaxWaitMs runs
  out, looped to a deadline. With the wait for a topic's leader
  (Kafka.IntegrationTests), the only places the suites wait on time.

  Ports: KAFKA_TEST_SASL_PORT (9096), KAFKA_TEST_SASL_TLS_PORT (9097),
  KAFKA_TEST_REAUTH_PORT (9098), KAFKA_TEST_PORT (9092), host
  KAFKA_TEST_HOST (localhost).

  DUnitX master: the FPCUnit mirror in tests/Integration/fpc is generated by
  tools/gen_fpc_mirror.py. }

interface

uses
  fpcunit, testregistry,
  SysUtils,
  PascalCommon.Utf8,
  PascalCommon.Threading,
  Kafka.Types,
  Kafka.Errors,
  Kafka.Protocol.Primitives,
  Kafka.Sasl,
  Kafka.Messages.Metadata,
  Kafka.Connection,
  Kafka.Cluster,
  Kafka.Producer,
  Kafka.Consumer,
  Kafka.TestHelpers;

type
  TKafkaSaslListener = (kslSasl, kslSaslTls, kslReauth, kslPlaintext);

  TKafkaSaslIntegrationTests = class(TTestCase)
  private
    FConnection: TKafkaConnection;
    FCluster: TKafkaCluster;
    FProducer: TKafkaProducer;
    FConsumer: TKafkaConsumer;
    FWaiter: TKafkaConsumer;
    function Params(AListener: TKafkaSaslListener;
      AMechanism: TKafkaSaslMechanism): TKafkaConnectionParams;
    function Bootstrap(AListener: TKafkaSaslListener): string;
    function NewProducer(AListener: TKafkaSaslListener;
      AMechanism: TKafkaSaslMechanism): TKafkaProducer;
    function NewConsumer(AListener: TKafkaSaslListener;
      AMechanism: TKafkaSaslMechanism): TKafkaConsumer;
    procedure ProduceAndConsume(AListener: TKafkaSaslListener; AMechanism: TKafkaSaslMechanism);
    function OpenFails(const AParams: TKafkaConnectionParams; out ACode: Int16): string;
    procedure CallMetadata;
    /// Polls FConsumer until a record whose value is AValue comes; False
    /// after ATimeoutMs.
    function PollFor(const AValue: string; ATimeoutMs: Cardinal): Boolean;
    /// Lets time pass until PcTickMs reaches ATick (the unit's header).
    procedure WaitUntil(ATick: UInt64);
  protected
    procedure TearDown; override;
  published
    procedure SaslPlaintext_Plain_ProducesAndConsumes;
    procedure SaslPlaintext_Scram_ProducesAndConsumes;
    procedure SaslSsl_Plain_ProducesAndConsumes;
    procedure SaslSsl_Scram_ProducesAndConsumes;
    procedure Plain_WrongPassword_IsAuthenticationFailed;
    procedure Scram_WrongPassword_IsAuthenticationFailed;
    procedure SaslClientOnThePlaintextListener_IsIllegalSaslState;
